WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.700
So how does

2
00:00:00.700 --> 00:00:02.140
it actually work?

3
00:00:02.140 --> 00:00:02.840
Picture a staff member

4
00:00:02.840 --> 00:00:03.440
with a new

5
00:00:03.440 --> 00:00:04.460
project folder.

6
00:00:04.460 --> 00:00:05.400
Promise Ledger takes it

7
00:00:05.400 --> 00:00:07.920
through seven steps. Collect.

8
00:00:07.920 --> 00:00:08.960
Staff gather the records

9
00:00:08.960 --> 00:00:10.360
for one project.

10
00:00:10.360 --> 00:00:12.200
Reports, letters, slides,

11
00:00:12.200 --> 00:00:13.720
minutes. Read.

12
00:00:13.720 --> 00:00:15.100
AI reads the documents

13
00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:16.260
finds the sentences that

14
00:00:16.260 --> 00:00:17.390
sound like promises.

15
00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:19.400
Check. Code confirms

16
00:00:19.400 --> 00:00:20.580
each quote appears,

17
00:00:20.580 --> 00:00:21.300
word for word,

18
00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:21.800
on the page

19
00:00:21.800 --> 00:00:22.680
it cites.

20
00:00:22.680 --> 00:00:23.720
If it doesn't match,

21
00:00:23.720 --> 00:00:25.440
it's dropped. Organize.

22
00:00:25.440 --> 00:00:26.200
Promises are sorted

23
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:26.880
by stage,

24
00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:29.240
from proposed to signed

25
00:00:29.240 --> 00:00:30.740
missing terms are flagged.

26
00:00:30.740 --> 00:00:31.820
Review. A person

27
00:00:31.820 --> 00:00:32.940
reads each item

28
00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:34.360
decides its status.

29
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:35.760
The AI never does.

30
00:00:35.760 --> 00:00:36.600
Share. The result

31
00:00:36.600 --> 00:00:37.720
is a one-page receipt

32
00:00:37.720 --> 00:00:39.500
that anyone can read.

33
00:00:39.500 --> 00:00:41.160
Watch. Reminders flag yearly

34
00:00:41.160 --> 00:00:42.260
checks end dates

35
00:00:42.260 --> 00:00:43.040
so they don't

36
00:00:43.040 --> 00:00:44.070
slip by unnoticed.

37
00:00:44.620 --> 00:00:45.500
Seven steps,

38
00:00:45.500 --> 00:00:46.410
one clear record.

